'''''Magnolia compressa''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Magnoliaceae]], native to [[Yunnan]], Taiwan, the [[Ryukyu Islands]], and southwest Japan, and introduced to South Korea.<ref name="554664-1" >{{cite web |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:554664-1 |title=''Magnolia compressa'' Maxim. |author=<!--Not stated--> |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Board of Trustees of the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew |access-date=8 September 2021 }}</ref> A small tree when in cultivation, it is hardy only to [[Hardiness zone|USDA zone 10]]. It may be planted in containers and brought indoors in the winter.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=282545 |title=''Magnolia compressa'' |author=<!--Not stated--> |date= |website=Plant Finder |publisher=Missouri Botanical Garden |access-date=8 September 2021 }}</ref>
